<article class="env-lemma" id="04NQ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04NQ">Lemma <span data-tag="04NQ">67.34.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Let $x \in |X|$. Assume $f$ is locally of finite type. Then we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \begin{matrix}  \text{relative dimension of }f\text{ at }x 

\\  = 

\\  \text{dimension of local ring of the fibre of }f\text{ at }x 

\\  + 

\\  \text{transcendence degree of }x/f(x) 

\end{matrix}  \]
</div>
  <p> where the notation is as in Definition <a href="/tag/04NM" data-tag="04NM">67.33.1</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows immediately from Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/02FX" data-tag="02FX">29.29.1</a> applied to $h : U \to V$ and $u \in U$ as in Lemma <a href="/tag/04NC" data-tag="04NC">67.22.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>